From: Zhivko Kocev <zikekocev57@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: use the requested handle for Read Encryption Key Size

The Realtek UART Bluetooth chip in a Nexbox A95X-B7N (HCI revision
0x365d, LMP subversion 0x462e) answers Read Encryption Key Size for a
second ACL link with the handle of the other link (btmon, shortened):

  < HCI Command: Read Encryption Key Size (0x05|0x0008) plen 2
          Handle: 6
        Read Encryption Key Size (0x05|0x0008) ncmd 2
          Status: Success (0x00)
          Handle: 4
          Key size: 16

read_enc_key_size_complete() looks the connection up by the handle in
the reply, so it updates link 4 again and never calls hci_encrypt_cfm()
for link 6. That link stays in BT_CONFIG and bluetoothd's service search
on it times out, so a second device never works while the first one is
connected.

Use the handle from the command that was sent. The key size from the
reply is kept, so a short key still fails l2cap_check_enc_key_size().
Controllers that answer with the right handle are not affected.

A reply that only arrives after the command timeout, while a key size
read for another link is pending, is now attributed to that link.

Signed-off-by: Zhivko Kocev <zikekocev57@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
@@ -2547,6 +2547,7 @@
 				       u16 opcode, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	const struct hci_rp_read_enc_key_size *rp;
+	const struct hci_cp_read_enc_key_size *cp;
 	struct hci_conn *conn;
 	u16 handle;
 
@@ -2561,6 +2562,19 @@
 	rp = (void *)skb->data;
 	handle = le16_to_cpu(rp->handle);
 
+	/* Some controllers (seen on a Realtek UART chip) answer with the
+	 * handle of a different connection once more than one ACL link
+	 * exists. The link we asked about would then never leave BT_CONFIG,
+	 * so use the handle from our own command. The reported key size is
+	 * kept, so a short key still fails the usual check.
+	 */
+	cp = hci_sent_cmd_data(hdev, HCI_OP_READ_ENC_KEY_SIZE);
+	if (cp && le16_to_cpu(cp->handle) != handle) {
+		BT_ERR("%s key size reply for handle %u, requested %u",
+		       hdev->name, handle, le16_to_cpu(cp->handle));
+		handle = le16_to_cpu(cp->handle);
+	}
+
 	hci_dev_lock(hdev);
 
 	conn = hci_conn_hash_lookup_handle(hdev, handle);
